{"text":"{
  "status": "NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT",
  "core_findings": [
    "Module correctness checks pass in all four categories, but generated-predictor parity remains unverified. Electronics has the weakest sampled training separability: pos_neg_margin_p10=0.1141 and pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate=0.0768; CDs_and_Vinyl has the strongest, at 1.1172 and 0.0058 respectively.",
    "Across categories, removing latest items increases sampled target rank by 3.64–6.98 positions versus 0.48–0.70 for removing oldest items; shuffle_older increases rank by 2.34–4.14. These describe reliance on fixed training histories and candidates, with 256 anonymous prefixes per category and no user-bootstrap intervals."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "Scores depend more on recent observed items than on the oldest items, while older-item order also affects rankings; these perturbations establish neither causal effects nor validation accuracy.",
    "Embedding_collapse_score ranges from 0.5719 to 0.6957, indicating directional concentration, strongest in Electronics; it does not measure recommendation diversity.",
    "Prefix memorization and sparse strata limit generalization of these findings, and deployment consistency remains unresolved until generated-predictor parity is established."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": 0.1903,
      "CDs_and_Vinyl:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": 0.0298,
      "Electronics:remove_latest.delta_rank.mean": 6.98046875,
      "Electronics:remove_oldest.delta_rank.mean": 0.671875,
      "Electronics:embedding_collapse_score": 0.6957
    },
    "brief_metric_read": {
      "pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "Training margins below 0.5; Electronics has more weakly separated sampled pairs.",
      "history_perturbations": "Descriptive means over anonymous prefixes; user identities and user-bootstrap intervals unavailable.",
      "correctness_audit": "Module and checkpoint roundtrip checks pass; generated writer and routing parity unavailable."
    }
  }
}"}
